"comparison": "Intel discloses a strategic shift to expand its internal manufacturing capabilities into an external foundry business to utilize high capital investments in leading-edge nodes like Intel 18A, whereas NVIDIA explicitly employs a fabless strategy to avoid the significant costs and risks associated with owning manufacturing operations. Intel states, \"The very high capital requirements of modern leading-edge semiconductor process technology... require us to expand the use of our process technologies... and grow the number of wafers produced beyond the expected growth for our own products\" (intc_2024_1_P014_S002), while NVIDIA notes, \"We utilize a fabless and contracting manufacturing strategy... we can avoid many of the significant costs and risks associated with owning and operating manufacturing operations\" (nvda_2024_1_P043_S001).",
