"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both companies leverage intellectual property as a strategic asset through licensing, though Intel's IP strategy is specifically tied to its foundry differentiation by including x86 cores in its IP portfolio, while NVIDIA focuses on broader technology access for custom development. Intel plans to differentiate its foundry offerings through \"a world-class IP portfolio that will include x86 cores\" (intc_2024_1_P014_S006). Similarly, NVIDIA states, \"We believe our IP is a valuable asset that can be accessed by our customers and partners through license and development agreements when they desire to build such capabilities directly into their own products\" (nvda_2024_1_P038_S002).",
